    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43706" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sēpĭa</span></b> , ae,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σηπία</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the cuttle-fish</i>,
			having a black, inky liquid, <i><span class="en">Cic. N.
				D. 2, 50, 127</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 9, 29, 45, § 84</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Plaut. Rud. 3, 2, 45</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 6, 17,
				7</span></i>.—This liquid was used for ink, <i><span class="en">Pers. 3,
			13</span></i>; hence, transf., <i>ink</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">furva,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Ep. 4, 76</span></i>
			.</div>
